akari (0.16.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The console on the machine runs in kmscon with MesloLGS NF: the
    prompt's symbols, 256 colours and Akari's mark in colour. The keyboard
    is the system's; without DRM, agetty takes over. kmscon and libtsm4
    come from trixie-backports through Akari's archive.
  * The QR code at the console has the same margin on every side.
  * /etc/issue stays Debian's (akari-base greets before login); the
    diversion from 0.15 is undone.

 -- Akari OS <packages@lucya.systems>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100

akari (0.15.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * One owner for everything: the containers lucya-aio makes for Lucent
    are shown in Docker, not changed there; Akari keeps lucya-aio itself
    up to date. Paired with the Lucent here: no setup code, no removing it;
    paired with one elsewhere: no second Lucent.
  * Caddy's door :8131 answers only this machine and Docker's networks.
  * Akari OS is no longer a container of Lucent's store.
  * The console: Akari's mark and the machine's name before login, a
    welcome with address, load, memory, disk, updates, Docker and Lucent
    after it. Debian's uname line, motd and issue are diverted.
  * akari-console-font gives the console font ▀ and ▄, which Debian's
    fonts lack: the QR code at the console works again.

 -- Akari OS <packages@lucya.systems>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100

akari (0.14.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Docker: a new app to manage containers. Containers grouped by Compose
    project with start, stop, restart, pause and remove; details with
    load, environment (secrets hidden) and a live log; new containers
    from a form, with system folders and Docker's socket kept out;
    images, volumes, networks and clean-up. Docker installs from Debian
    with one click. Only for accounts that manage.
  * Lucent with one click: Akari starts lucya-aio, shows Lucent's address
    and setup code, and fills in the pairing. Caddy opens :8131 for
    Lucent's tool API only, without TLS, for a Lucent on the same machine.
  * Lucent's status page for Akari works again, and shows and installs
    updates.

 -- Akari OS <packages@lucya.systems>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0100

akari (0.13.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Settings for the real system: network, date and time (time zone,
    network time), the machine (name, processor, disks, restart, power
    off) and updates with apt, which run in a unit of their own.
  * The start menu: pinned apps, places, recent files and every app from
    A to Z; restart and power off for accounts that manage.
  * Programs from outside Debian (Spotify and others that register with
    xdg-desktop-menu) show up: akari-desktop brings xdg-utils and the
    folders it needs.
  * New app icons in Facet's glass.
  * Spectrum: one pastel rainbow over the whole desk.
  * Rounder corners; the taskbar grows with an opening app; larger dock
    icons; the desktop as an icon; magnification off until switched on.

 -- Akari OS <packages@lucya.systems>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100

akari (0.12.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Akari on the phone and as a web app: a home screen with the apps,
    full-screen windows with back and close, popovers as sheets, safe
    areas; manifest and icons to add it to the home screen (iOS, Android).
  * Taskbar: the apps pill never shrinks, the status pill gives way in two
    steps; the width animation clips sideways; the glass rim has no seam;
    no hover that sticks on touch.
  * Rainbow and spectrum tint: the glass no longer freezes on WebKit
    (Safari, iPad, iPhone).
  * Facet as the reference: corners by role, spacing from the scale, hover
    as a colour step instead of a lift, no glow.

